description:
ISO 10303-21 §6.2 allows arbitrary whitespace (including newlines) between records; the record terminator is the `;`, and what follows is lexically free until the next record's leading token. A producer that emits each record on its own line plus a trailing blank line (`..);

`) is technically conformant but stresses streaming tokenisers that special-case `;
` as a "next record starts here" boundary. Mixing `;
` and `;

` and `; #NEXT=` (no separator) within the same DATA section is non-canonical: a strict tokeniser that picks one form may mis-frame the others. Bug-reporter language: "STEP file has blank lines between records", "extra newlines confuse parser", "EOR formatting inconsistent across DATA section".

